    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Tangent: $y=\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac23$. At $x=8$, both the curve and tangent give $y=2$, so they meet again at $(8,2)$.",
      "worked": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-answer-derivative",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac13x^{-2/3}\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3x^{2/3}}\\end{aligned}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-answer-gradient",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "At T(−1, −1):",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{1}{3(-1)^{2/3}}\\\\&=\\frac13\\end{aligned}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-answer-tangent",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Tangent equation at T(−1, −1):",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}y-(-1)&=\\frac13\\bigl(x-(-1)\\bigr)\\\\y&=\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac23\\end{aligned}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-answer-intersection",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Find the intersection with the curve:",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\sqrt[3]{x}=\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac23",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-answer-check",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Substitute ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x=8",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " into both sides:",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}\\text{LHS}&=\\sqrt[3]{8}=2\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac83-\\frac23=2\\end{aligned}",
                "display": true
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Hence (8, 2) is a point of intersection distinct from T.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-extension-answer",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Extension students may be asked the same question without being given the coordinates; to do so, solve the equation by cubing both sides.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-extension-cubing",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}x&=\\left(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac23\\right)^3\\\\x&=\\frac1{27}(x-2)^3\\end{aligned}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p69-q10-extension-factorisation",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Expanding and moving all terms to one side:",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "-x^3+6x^2+15x+8=0",
                "display": true
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Using the factor theorem, ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "P(8)=0",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", so ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x=8",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " gives a point of intersection. In fact,",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}-(x-8)(x+1)^2&=0\\\\x&=8\\text{ or }-1\\end{aligned}",
                "display": true
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The repeated root −1 corresponds to the tangent point T; the other intersection is (8, 2).",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
